# shellcheck shell=bash
# .envrc - direnv entrypoint: activate the mise toolchain, then hydrate .kit/ (sourced by direnv)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# direnv runs this on cd, so a desk that uses direnv instead of `mise activate` gets the same two things that shell
# does: the pinned tools and kit/bin on PATH from mise.toml, and what the kit places under .kit/ in place, quietly
# when it already is. mise's own enter hook runs only under `mise activate`; this is its direnv counterpart.

use mise
kit hydrate --quick

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
